            <ArticleTitle>Reflections From the Other Side: The Refugee Journey to Health and Well-Being.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>283-288</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1891/1078-4535.22.4.283</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The refugee crisis is an urgent global health issue; the number of displaced people has escalated to its worst point in recorded history. To explore the refugee phenomenon as a social determinant of health, this article examines the experience of Somali refugees in Minnesota. Health care barriers unique to refugees are explored through the firstperson perspective of one Somali woman who ultimately became a nurse.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
